# Catch / client machine — credentials

Canonical always-apply rule: [`.cursor/rules/catch_client_credentials.mdc`](../../.cursor/rules/catch_client_credentials.mdc)  
Full session context: [CATCH_MACHINE_CURSOR_CONTEXT.md](../product/CATCH_MACHINE_CURSOR_CONTEXT.md)

## Protect developer GitHub (critical)

Developer GitHub has **other important projects**. Catch’s machine must **never** hold developer GitHub auth.

- Public `git clone` / `git pull` only — no `gh auth login`, PAT, or developer SSH.
- Code on developer Mac → push; Catch only pull.
- Do not sign Cursor into the developer account on Catch’s PC.

## Hugging Face (OK for this project)

Weights-only for Phase 1. Prefer **Tailscale+SSH** (`scripts/pull_from_catch.sh`) or AnyDesk `.pth` transfer. If HF on Catch: read-only scoped token, then `unset HF_TOKEN` before leaving. Never paste write tokens into chat or docs.

## Mac ↔ Catch files

Default: **Tailscale + SSH key** — [CATCH_MAC_FILE_SYNC.md](../product/CATCH_MAC_FILE_SYNC.md). Stage on Catch `~/soccer_exchange/from_catch/`; Mac `bash scripts/pull_from_catch.sh`. No `catch` password if pub key pasted in `authorized_keys` via AnyDesk.
